# Counts below are for the full demo dataset (mining.ttl + generated.ttl). The
# generated sites and boreholes contribute additional matches; the named sites are
# the ones placed deliberately to demonstrate the behaviour.
# A query polygon with an interior ring. Rings after the first are holes and they are
# honoured, so a shape falling inside the hole does not match.
#
# The outer ring covers Kalgoorlie; the hole is drawn over the two Datum Demo points.
#
# 4 rows, including site-excised-tenement and site-legacy-survey, both in the ring body.
# Absent: site-datum-gda2020 and site-datum-crs84, which sit inside the hole.
#
# Delete the second ring and re-run: 4 rows becomes 6, and the two Datum Demo sites
# reappear. That contrast is the whole point of the query.
PREFIX luc: <urn:jena:lucene:index#>
SELECT ?entity ?score WHERE {
  (?hit ?entity ?score) luc:query ("default" "default" "*"
    '{"op":"s_intersects","args":[{"property":"urn:jena:lucene:field#location"},{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[121.40,-31.30],[121.80,-31.30],[121.80,-30.70],[121.40,-30.70],[121.40,-31.30]],[[121.60,-31.25],[121.72,-31.25],[121.72,-31.15],[121.60,-31.15],[121.60,-31.25]]]}]}'
    ""
    20
    0)
}
